-- int-tests-offence: headline (d), whole scenarios across groups G1 (the entity and whether it is a Jersey entity), G6 (the offences of Articles 19(11) and 20(6)), G7 (Articles 21 to 23, 37 and 38),
-- G8 (Articles 26 and 29) and G9 (the cap in Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f)).  EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from the Law before this module was run:
--   Article 21(3): a Jersey entity that is not a registered charity must not refer to itself, or cause or permit another to refer to it, as a "charity"; 21(10): an entity that contravenes (1), (3) or (5) is liable
--   to a fine of level 3. Article 21(4): a person who, knowing, suspecting or having reasonable grounds to suspect that the entity is a Jersey entity and is not a registered charity, calls it a "charity" intending
--   to induce a gift of property or financial advantage, contravenes (4); 21(9): an entity or other person that contravenes (2), (4) or (6) is liable to imprisonment for 2 years and a fine.
--   Article 37(1): if an offence by a partnership or body corporate is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of a partner, director, governor, secretary or similar officer, that person is also guilty
--   of the offence and liable to the penalty provided for it; the unincorporated association is not named (trap T26).
--   Article 19(11): a person who without reasonable excuse contravenes 19(10) is liable to imprisonment for one year and a fine; Article 20(6): contravening a disqualification order, 2 years and a fine;
--   Article 26(7): 3 months and level 3; Article 26(10): 2 years and a fine; Article 29(1): 2 years and a fine. Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f): Regulations may carry a penalty not exceeding 2 years and a fine.

§ `Integration layer -- headline (d): scenarios`

