§§ `D8: the day -- the offences of Part 6 begin on 1 January 2019, those of Article 19(11) on 1 May 2018`

-- Article 21 was brought into force with the remainder on 1 January 2019. On 31 December 2018 the gate refuses on the first Article of the list that is not in force, Article 21.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2018 12 31) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the company calls itself a charity`, officer IS NOTHING) BECAUSE "Article 21 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 6) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 January 2019"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the governor acts a month after reporting`, officer IS NOTHING) BECAUSE "Article 19 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 5) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"

§§ `D9: "a person", "the entity" and "another person" -- Articles 21(1), 21(2) and 21(7) (the parties of a statement are separate values; assumed, not ruled, 2026-10-27)`

-- The Law (src:533-561).  21(1): an entity that is not a registered charity (a) must not refer to itself as being registered by the Commissioner and (b) must not cause or permit ANOTHER person to refer to it so.
-- 21(2): a PERSON must not refer to an unregistered entity as registered, if the person (a) knows, suspects or has reasonable grounds to suspect that it is not a registered charity and (b) intends, by so referring, to cause
-- ANOTHER person to be misled as to the nature of the entity or to give it property or a financial or other advantage.  21(7): paragraphs (2), (4) and (6) apply whether or not the person making the reference is also the entity.
-- 21(9): contravening (2) is punishable by imprisonment for 2 years (24 months) and a fine; 21(10): contravening (1) by a fine of level 3.
-- EXPECTED VALUES decided by hand from those words before the module was run:
--   * A person who intends only to mislead THEMSELF does not intend to cause ANOTHER person to be misled: 21(2) is not contravened.  If the entity did not cause or permit the statement and the maker is not the entity, no other
--     paragraph reaches it either (21(1)(a) needs the entity as the maker, 21(1)(b) needs the entity to have caused or permitted it): no offence, no penalty.  If the entity DID cause or permit it, 21(1)(b) still catches the act: a fine
--     of level 3 and no imprisonment.  The same intent against a donor, who is another person, makes out 21(2): 24 months and a fine (the control that shows the distinctness is what changes the answer).
--   * The entity itself, knowing, saying it is registered with intent to mislead a donor: 21(1)(a) (strict) and, by 21(7), 21(2): both are made out (F7.4, favoured), so the penalties are a fine of level 3 and 24 months and a fine,
--     and an officer who connived is guilty of both, because the knowing offence is the body's own when the entity made the statement (the director of D2, whose statement was made by a third person, is guilty of the strict offence only).
--   * 21(1)(b): the entity caused or permitted a person other than itself to say it: (b) is made out, (a) is not.  The entity itself saying it, even if it also caused or permitted the saying: (a) is made out and (b) is not,
--     because the maker is not "another person"; a single contravention of paragraph (1), one fine of level 3.
GIVETH AN `Intent of the person making a statement`
`d9 an intent to mislead the other person only` MEANS
    `Intent of the person making a statement` WITH
        `to cause the other person to be misled as to the nature of the entity` IS TRUE
        `to cause the other person to give the entity any property` IS FALSE
        `to cause the other person to give the entity a financial advantage` IS FALSE
        `to cause the other person to give the entity some other advantage` IS FALSE

GIVETH AN `Intent of the person making a statement`
`d9 no intent` MEANS
    `Intent of the person making a statement` WITH
        `to cause the other person to be misled as to the nature of the entity` IS FALSE
        `to cause the other person to give the entity any property` IS FALSE
        `to cause the other person to give the entity a financial advantage` IS FALSE
        `to cause the other person to give the entity some other advantage` IS FALSE

GIVETH AN `Awareness of the person making a statement`
`d9 knowledge that the entity is not a registered charity` MEANS
    `Awareness of the person making a statement` WITH
        `that the entity is not a registered charity` IS `Int fx knowledge`
        `that the entity is a Jersey entity` IS `Int fx no awareness`
        `that the entity is neither a Jersey entity nor an excepted foreign charity` IS `Int fx no awareness`
        `that the entity does not meet all of the conditions of Article 23(3)` IS `Int fx no awareness`

GIVETH AN `Awareness of the person making a statement`
`d9 no awareness` MEANS
    `Awareness of the person making a statement` WITH
        `that the entity is not a registered charity` IS `Int fx no awareness`
        `that the entity is a Jersey entity` IS `Int fx no awareness`
        `that the entity is neither a Jersey entity nor an excepted foreign charity` IS `Int fx no awareness`
        `that the entity does not meet all of the conditions of Article 23(3)` IS `Int fx no awareness`

-- A statement that the entity is registered by the Commissioner, in connection with an activity in Jersey, with no prescribed exception.
GIVEN maker IS A Party @desc The person making the statement
      other IS A Party @desc The other person, whom the maker intends to mislead or to get something from
      caused IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity caused or permitted another person to make the statement
      awareness IS AN `Awareness of the person making a statement` @desc What the maker knew
      intent IS AN `Intent of the person making a statement` @desc What the maker intended
GIVETH A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23`
`d9 a statement that the entity is registered, by` maker other caused awareness intent MEANS
    `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` WITH
        `what is said of the entity` IS `that it is registered by the Commissioner`
        `in connection with an activity of the entity in Jersey` IS TRUE
        `the entity as a party` IS `Int fx the party standing for the entity`
        `the person making the statement` IS maker
        `the other person` IS other
        `the entity caused or permitted another person to make it` IS caused
        `an exception prescribed under Article 21(8) applies` IS FALSE
        `an exception prescribed under Article 23(4) applies` IS FALSE
        awareness IS awareness
        intent IS intent

GIVEN statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement
GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`d9 the act of` statement MEANS
    `a statement about an entity` WITH
        body IS `the unregistered Jersey company`
        `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS `the facts of a Jersey body for Article 22`
        `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS TRUE
        statement IS statement

GIVEN statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement
GIVETH AN `Offence case`
`d9 the case of` statement MEANS `Offence case` WITH act IS `d9 the act of` statement, officer IS NOTHING

-- The company as an Entity (for the paragraph-level Booleans); it is not on the register.
GIVETH AN Entity
`d9 the company as an entity` MEANS `Int IP5 the entity` fleet `the text of 2 October 2026` EMPTY (YMD 2026 10 2) `the unregistered Jersey company`

-- sA: a third person P says the entity is registered, knowing it is not, meaning only to mislead P (the other person IS the maker); the entity did not cause or permit it.
GIVETH A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23`
`d9 sA` MEANS `d9 a statement that the entity is registered, by` `Int fx a third person` `Int fx a third person` FALSE `d9 knowledge that the entity is not a registered charity` `d9 an intent to mislead the other person only`
-- sA2: as sA, but the entity caused or permitted P to say it.
GIVETH A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23`
`d9 sA2` MEANS `d9 a statement that the entity is registered, by` `Int fx a third person` `Int fx a third person` TRUE `d9 knowledge that the entity is not a registered charity` `d9 an intent to mislead the other person only`
-- sA3: as sA, but the person they mean to mislead is a donor, another person.
GIVETH A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23`
`d9 sA3` MEANS `d9 a statement that the entity is registered, by` `Int fx a third person` `Int fx a donor` FALSE `d9 knowledge that the entity is not a registered charity` `d9 an intent to mislead the other person only`
-- sB: the entity itself says it is registered, knowing it is not, meaning to mislead a donor (Article 21(7)).
GIVETH A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23`
`d9 sB` MEANS `d9 a statement that the entity is registered, by` `Int fx the party standing for the entity` `Int fx a donor` FALSE `d9 knowledge that the entity is not a registered charity` `d9 an intent to mislead the other person only`
-- sC1: the entity caused or permitted a third person to say it; no awareness and no intent.
GIVETH A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23`
`d9 sC1` MEANS `d9 a statement that the entity is registered, by` `Int fx a third person` `Int fx a donor` TRUE `d9 no awareness` `d9 no intent`
-- sC2: the entity itself says it, and also caused or permitted it; no awareness and no intent.
GIVETH A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23`
`d9 sC2` MEANS `d9 a statement that the entity is registered, by` `Int fx the party standing for the entity` `Int fx a donor` TRUE `d9 no awareness` `d9 no intent`
-- sC3: a third person says it, the entity neither caused nor permitted it; no awareness and no intent.
GIVETH A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23`
`d9 sC3` MEANS `d9 a statement that the entity is registered, by` `Int fx a third person` `Int fx a donor` FALSE `d9 no awareness` `d9 no intent`

GIVETH AN `Offence case`
`d9 the case of the connivance of a director in sB` MEANS
    `Offence case` WITH act IS `d9 the act of` `d9 sB`, officer IS JUST (`Int fx an officer who connived, of` `a body corporate` `a director of the body corporate`)

-- (1) A person who means only to mislead themself.
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`d9 the case of` `d9 sA`))'s `an offence is made out`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`d9 the case of` `d9 sA`))'s penalties EQUALS EMPTY
